go 1.25.0

// The workspace composes the SDK and the product modules from source during
// local development, so a change to the SDK is testable before it is tagged.
//
// The replacement below is a release bootstrap and is temporary. The SDK
// release gate compares its tag against the version modules/reference requires,
// so that requirement has to name v0.2.0 before sdk/v0.2.0 exists — and the Go
// tool cannot build a module graph that requires a version with no revision, so
// without this every build in the repository fails rather than only the ones
// that exercise the module. The workspace carried exactly this until sdk/v0.1.0
// was published.
//
// Drop it once sdk/v0.2.0 is pushed. The window it covers is described in
// docs/reference/release-artifacts.md under "Releasing a version nothing is
// built against yet". TestTheReferenceModuleWorksFromAnotherRepository is
// deliberately not covered by it: that test is defined by GOWORK=off, so it
// resolves the SDK from the proxy the way a product team's own repository does,
// and it skips itself until the tag exists.
//
// Committed replace directives remain prohibited in every go.mod; the workspace
// is the sanctioned place for one. See docs/plans/first-cli-vertical-slice.md
// section 4 and docs/adr/0009-sdk-versioning-and-publication.md.
use (
	.
	./modules/reference
	./sdk
)

replace github.com/wso2/wso2-cli/sdk v0.2.0 => ./sdk
